[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      ### Bug 2 — `test_slugify_collapses_repeated_separators` (`src/text_utils.py:20`)

[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      **Actual:** `slugify("hello   world!!!")` → `"hello--world"`  
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      **Expected:** `"hello-world"`

[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      **Root cause:** Three spaces become three `-` chars in `result_chars`, yielding `collapsed = "hello---world"`. Then `.strip("-")` does nothing (no leading/trailing hyphen). Then `.replace("--", "-")` only eliminates one pair of the overlapping `--` occurrences in `"---"` — Python's `str.replace` finds non-overlapping matches, so `"---"` has only one non-overlapping match (positions 5-6), leaving the third `-` as a sibling to produce `"hello--world"`.

[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      **Fix:** Replace line 20's replacement logic; `"--".replace` is insufficient for runs of 3+ hyphens. Change from:
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      ```python
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      return collapsed.strip("-").replace("--", "-")
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      ```
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      to:
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      ```python
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      result = collapsed.strip("-")
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      return "-".join(filter(None, result.split("-")))
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      ```
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      This splits on any hyphen run and rejoins with a single hyphen — no import needed, works for any run length.

[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      ---

[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      ### Bug 3 — `test_truncate_respects_max_len_including_suffix` (`src/text_utils.py:28`)

[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      **Actual:** `truncate("The quick brown fox", max_len=10)` → `"The quick …"` (11 chars — the suffix overflows)  
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      **Expected:** output length ≤ 10

[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      **Root cause:** Line 28 slices `text[:max_len]` (10 chars) then appends `"…"` on top, yielding `max_len + len(suffix)` total chars. The suffix length is not subtracted from the slice.

[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      **Fix:** Change line 28 from:
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      ```python
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      return text[:max_len] + suffix
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      ```
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      to:
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      ```python
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      return text[:max(0, max_len - len(suffix))] + suffix
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      ```
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      `max(0, ...)` prevents a negative slice when `max_len < len(suffix)`, which would wrap around via Python's negative-index semantics.

[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      ---

[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      ### Summary of exact changes to `src/text_utils.py`

[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      | Line | Current | Replace with |
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      |------|---------|--------------|
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      | 14 | `result_chars.append(char)` | `result_chars.append(char.lower())` |
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      | 20 | `return collapsed.strip("-").replace("--", "-")` | `result = collapsed.strip("-")\nreturn "-".join(filter(None, result.split("-")))` |
[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      | 28 | `return text[:max_len] + suffix` | `return text[:max(0, max_len - len(suffix))] + suffix` |

[generalist:kind-leaf-8672]      All three changes are localized to `src/text_utils.py`. No tests are modified. No new imports are required.
